      "writtenOn": "2024-12-04T07:32:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "framework-X-pre-jarjar is basically framework-X.impl, but before the jarjar step. It\u0027s generated separately via common java_defaults.\n\nIt is not possible to use framework-X-pre-jarjar to generate framework-X.impl, because a java_sdk_library needs sources to generate stubs, so it can\u0027t include it as a static_lib.\nAnd it shouldn\u0027t be included as-is in the APEX: the jarjared version of it (framework-X.impl) needs to be included instead.\n\nThe design is a bit complicated but I don\u0027t think we have an alternative right now; it would probably be best to avoid back-and-forth.\n\nIf we mark the dependency as \"installable: false\", would that fix the problem ?\nIdeally as I mentioned in the other comment, the java_sdk_library would take care of generating the pre-jarjar version by itself so it\u0027s not a separate build rule. But the checker shouldn\u0027t block development if it doesn\u0027t support a use-case that doesn\u0027t have supported alternatives today.",
      "parentUuid": "e2f9915c_52020572",
      "revId": "e078dbf6579f5ebf45228a24727a64bd75d1869b",
